<content>
  <section><title>Find the \(x\)-Intercepts</title>
<para>The \(x\)-intercepts of the graph of an equation occur when \(y = 0\).</para>
<para><emphasis>Example 1</emphasis></para>
<para>For the equation \(y=(x-9)(x+2)\), look at the factors \((x-9)\) and \((x+2)\).</para>
<para>\(y=(9-9)(9+2)\)</para>
<para>Notice in the second factor, \((x+2)\), \(x=-2\) makes the factor equal to 0.</para>
<para>\(y=(-2-9)(-2+2)\)</para>
<para>In the equation \(y=(x-9)(x+2)\), \(y=0\) when \(x=9\) and \(x=-2\).</para>
<para><emphasis>Example 2</emphasis></para>
<para>Find the \(x\)-intercepts for \(y=(2x+7)(x-4)\).</para>
<para>The \(x\)-intercepts occur when \(y = 0\).</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}2x+7&amp;=&amp;0\;\;\;\;\;x-4&amp;=&amp;0\\x&amp;=&amp;-3.5\;\;\;\;\;\;x&amp;=&amp;4\end{array}\)</para>
<title>Try It: Find the \(x\)-Intercepts</title>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find the \(x\)-intercepts for \(y=(2x-5)(x+3)\).</para>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Here is how to find the \(x\)-intercepts:</para>
  <para>The \(x\)-intercepts occur when \(y = 0\).</para>
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}2x-5&amp;=&amp;0\;\;\;\;\;x+3&amp;=&amp;0\\x&amp;=&amp;2.5\;\;\;\;\;\;x&amp;=&amp;-3\end{array}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><title>Check Your Understanding</title>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="38be50d7-2d77-4cfd-87ad-c509b2f0e653" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"> ----------------------------------------

  <!--Q#-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c70e3466-ddbb-46c7-8eb3-670add88a2bd" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(x = 3\), \(x = -0.5\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x = -3\\), \\(x = 0.5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 3\\), \\(x = -0.5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = -3\\), \\(x = 1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 3\\), \\(x = -1\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What are the \(x\)-intercept(s) of the graph of \(y=(2x+1)(x-3)\)?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->

